        459,
        768
      ],
      "margin_number": 1,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐκεῖνοσί Compare οὗτοί (line 20). ‘That is our master there.’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 13,
      "bbox": [
        465,
        168,
        479,
        768
      ],
      "margin_number": 4,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τῷ δὲ δεσπότῃ Possessive dative, see GE p. 180, #190 (b).",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 14,
      "bbox": [
        484,
        168,
        513,
        861
      ],
      "margin_number": 5,
      "speaker": "ἐπιθόμεθα",
      "text": "κελεύοντι ἐπιθόμεθα πείθομαι takes the dative; ἐπιθόμην is the second aorist. ‘We obeyed him ordering.’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 15,
      "bbox": [
        520,
        168,
        574,
        843
      ],
      "margin_number": 6,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐνέπεσεν For the principal parts of πίπτω see 9A line 17.\nἔγνω What is it? Aorist of γιγνώσκω γνώσομαι ἔγνων: see GE p. 201,\n#209.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 16,
      "bbox": [
        581,
        168,
        617,
        900
      ],
      "margin_number": 9,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ὑμεῖς δ᾽ ἀποκρίνεσθε ἡμῖν ἐρωτῶσιν Note the dative plural of the participle agreeing with ἡμῖν. ‘You answer us asking.’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 17,
      "bbox": [
        621,
        168,
        654,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": 16,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οὗτος δέ μοι ἐρομένῳ ἀποκρίνεται ‘This man answers me, having asked.’\nNote the aorist participle ἐρόμενος from ἐρωτάω ἐρωτήσω ἠρόμην.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 18,
      "bbox": [
        659,
        168,
        694,
        880
      ],
      "margin_number": 18,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "φιλόξενος ... Φιλόξενος This is the joke we have been working up to, with\nall the words beginning φιλ-, a pun on the name of Philoxenos.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 19,
      "bbox": [
        713,
        192,
        727,
        363
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Translation for 9B",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 20,
      "bbox": [
        735,
        90,
        867,
        906
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "XANTHIAS",
      "text": "That is our master there, who is sleeping above peacefully. Can’t you see him sleeping? So this is our master here. But the master has a very old father. The master ordered us to guard his father, and we obeyed his orders. For the master fell into perplexity about his father, since he knew that he was more wicked than the others in the city, and responsible for many evils. For the master’s father has a certain illness. So I ask you, spectators, what happens to be the name of this illness? You answer us asking. Come now, what does this man say?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 21,
      "bbox": [
        872,
        88,
        925,
        893
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "SOSIAS",
      "text": "He in answering us thinks that the old man is ‘a lover of dice’. But I say to the man that it is clear that he is speaking nonsense, answering such things. None the less ‘love-’ is the beginning of this evil.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    }
